! C22-6578 PROBLEM 3.6, "SCALAR PRODUCT OF VECTORS", printed p.30 (PDF
! 31), read in the ink.
!
!   "Find the following vector scalar product (a,b) = SUM(k = 0..16)
!   a(k) b(k) where a(k) is in A+K, b(k) in B+K, K = 0.0(1.0)16.0.  Put
!   the result in C."
!
!   Method 1.  Use LFT, *+.
!               LX, $3, SXTEEN
!               L(U), A
!               D*(N), B
!       LOFT    LFT(N), A($3)
!               *+(N), B($3)
!               CB+, $3, LOFT
!               SRD(N), C
!               BEW, $
!       SXTEEN  XW, 1.0, 16, $
!
! The nine printed statements are the deck's first nine, as printed.
! (The page leaves the first unnamed; the deck names it START so that
! END has somewhere to point.)  A, B and C are the deck's.
!
! ASSEMBLED WITH ASM=strap2, as the rest of Chapter 3 is.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE CLAIMS, comment (a): "The *+ operation yields a
! double-precision result."  The data is chosen so that a
! single-precision sum, a truncating store, and a rounding store give
! three different words.
!
! DATA.  a(0) = b(0) = 2**40 + 1;  a(1) = b(1) = 2**16;
!        a(k) = k, b(k) = (-1)**k k for k = 2..16.
!
! THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE HAND-DERIVED:
!   a(0) b(0) = 2**80 + 2**41 + 1         (D*, 96 bits: Ref. Man. p.97)
!   a(1) b(1) = 2**32
!   k = 2..16:  4 - 9 + 16 - 25 + ... + 256
!             = (4 + 16 + ... + 256) - (9 + 25 + ... + 225)
!             = 816 - 679 = 137
!   (a,b) = 2**80 + 2**41 + 2**32 + 138, an 81-bit integer.  Every
!   partial sum is an integer of at most 81 bits, the 96-bit fraction
!   holds it whole (MULTIPLY AND ADD, printed p.98: the 96-bit product
!   "remains unnormalized throughout the addition", then "an addition is
!   performed similar to that described in ADD DOUBLE"), so nothing is
!   lost before the store.
!   SRD(N), C (printed p.96): exponent 81; the 48 fraction bits are the
!   integer's bits 80-33, 800000000100 (2**80 and 2**41); the 49th bit
!   is the integer's bit 32, a one; "adding one to the fraction in the
!   accumulator in bit position 60" carries into the 48th:
!   800000000101.
!       C = exponent 81 (0A2), fraction 800000000101:  0A28000000001010
!   A truncating store would leave ...1000; a single-precision sum
!   would have lost the 2**32 and everything under it on the way.
!
!   acc_left: word 8 is accumulator bits 0-63 -- the exponent, the 48
!   unrounded bits and the first four of the low half, whose leading bit
!   is that same bit 32:                               0A28000000001008
!   FT: the factor register, word 14, holds the last LFT(N) operand,
!   a(16) = 16 = .1 x 2**5 (comment (b): "$FT is a bona fide memory
!   location"):                                        00A8000000000000
!
! tests/problem_3_expected.py (p36) gives the same three words.
!
! INJECTION, OBSERVED 2026-11-15 (data side, on a copy of the deck, the
! deck itself untouched): b(1) changed from 65536 to 65535, so the
! second product is 2**32 - 2**16, bit 32 of the sum is a zero and the
! store rounds down.  FAIL C (got 0a28000000001000) and acc_left (got
! 0a28000000001007); FT and the PC passed.

START   LX, $3, SXTEEN
        L(U), A
        D*(N), B
LOFT    LFT(N), A($3)
        *+(N), B($3)
        CB+, $3, LOFT
        SRD(N), C
        BEW, $
SXTEEN  XW, 1.0, 16, $
! --- the deck's data ------------------------------------------------
A       DD(N), 1099511627777, 65536, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9
        DD(N), 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16
B       DD(N), 1099511627777, 65536, 2, -3, 4, -5, 6, -7, 8, -9
        DD(N), 10, -11, 12, -13, 14, -15, 16
C       DR(N), (1)
        END, START
